From 2aa9ea562f0dac82e9ad9cffee144aee79ea745a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:24:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): an armed Boundary row takes viewport clicks in
 Models mode

With "Click selects" set to Models while "Do not touch" (or any other
Boundary row) showed "Picking...", a viewport click selected the whole
model and the row got no pick. `feature_routed` now also routes the click
through the feature pick while a Boundary row is armed; `ask` already
took faces and edges for it in every mode (#1727).

Pinned by do_not_touch_takes_viewport_clicks_in_models_mode (red before
the fix: "selected guard") and
do_not_touch_takes_a_face_and_an_edge_by_viewport_click, both on a 2D
Offset with real viewport clicks.

Fixes #3335

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
